ames. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vs. a music font.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changed two ways.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"title":"MXLPosition"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"url":"\/documentatio